# In S4, "life" is counted among the soul's functions, so "live well" in P3 and C1 means doing that function well.
# S16 reads "live well" as faring well, prospering. Only that reading licenses "blessed and happy".
# Unsure: "excellence" in P1 and P2 (functional excellence, as in S8) may also shift toward moral virtue in P4 (S12, where justice was earlier admitted to be "the excellence"). I judged it one sense because P4 simply identifies justice with that functional excellence.
